  "_comment_steps_assignedTo": "Team-member routing queries collectionGroup('steps').where('assignedTo','==',uid). A single-field COLLECTION query is auto-indexed, but the COLLECTION_GROUP scope needs an explicit field override (below) \u2014 it is NOT a composite index (Firestore rejects that as redundant).",
  "fieldOverrides": [
    {
      "collectionGroup": "steps",
      "fieldPath": "assignedTo",
      "indexes": [
        {
          "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "steps",
      "fieldPath": "assignedToUids",
      "indexes": [
        {
          "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        },
        {
          "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "_comment_steps_assignedToUids": "#192: a step may have several assignees. Team-member routing also queries collectionGroup('steps').where('assignedToUids','array-contains',uid), which needs an ARRAY_CONFIG CONTAINS override at COLLECTION_GROUP scope (an array-contains query cannot use the ASCENDING order index above)."
}
